    "reasoning": [
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "Alaska August 2026 ex parte renewal share"
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "The target is Alaska's state row for the August 2026 reporting cohort in dataset 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c, using the original O submission at first publication. All historical anchors use O rows and the same calculated share. Updated U submissions, national totals, and national weighted percentages are excluded."
      },
      {
        "kind": "tool",
        "tool": "official.lookup",
        "call": "curl -sS against the CMS datastore query endpoint for dataset 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c, limit 100, filtered to state_abbreviation=AK and original_or_updated=O; echo original numerator, total renewed, renewals due, and footnotes.",
        "result": "Fetched ex parte/total-renewed counts: June 2025 6246/8572; July 5742/9014; August 6339/9528; September 5397/8444; October 4587/8004; November 6026/9791; December 5547/8791. Earlier seasonal comparisons were June 2024 10258/12542 and August 2024 6879/9681. The response included Alaska O rows through June 2026."
      },
      {
        "kind": "tool",
        "tool": "official.lookup",
        "call": "curl -sS against the same CMS datastore endpoint, filtered to Alaska O rows with reporting_period>=202601, projecting reporting period, total renewed, and ex parte renewed.",
        "result": "Fetched six rows: January 2026 ex parte 3782, total renewed 7006; February 4686/8345; March 3712/7272; April 4719/7704; May 5505/8417; June 4303/7158. Calculated shares are 54.0%, 56.2%, 51.0%, 61.3%, 65.4%, and 60.1%."
      },
      {
        "kind": "tool",
        "tool": "official.lookup",
        "call": "Open the official June 2026 Eligibility Operations and Enrollment Snapshot, page index 30, and inspect Alaska's coverage retention and disenrollment table.",
        "result": "Alaska has 15924 renewals due, 45% total renewed, and 27% renewed on an ex parte basis. The table explicitly uses total renewals due as its percentage denominator. This differs from the successful-renewal share calculated here: 100*4303/7158=60.1146%, versus 100*4303/15924=27.0221%."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Resolver ambiguity: the ledger names an ex parte renewal share but leaves its denominator unspecified. I interpret share as the ex parte fraction of successful renewals. CMS's displayed ex parte rate instead divides by renewals due. These are materially different quantities; the supplied contract does not establish which denominator its automated resolver implements."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Publication-date verification gap: the official CMS release page lists June 2026 as released September 25, 2026, but provides no announcement confirming December 15, 2026 for August's original submission. I retain the registered resolutionDate without inferring a publication date from cadence. This run does not satisfy the requirement for official verification of that date."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "The outside-view base rate is the 13 monthly O-row shares from June 2025 through June 2026: their arithmetic mean is 61.3014%. The January\u2013June 2026 mean is 57.9921%, while June is 60.1146%. These fetched state observations anchor the forecast."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Level: blend June persistence with the recent six-month mean. Momentum: apply no extrapolated trend because the spring rise reversed in June. One-off effects: preserve the published counts despite ex parte undercount footnotes; no numerical correction is justified. Policy mechanism: apply no speculative automation adjustment. June-to-August declines in the two preceding years are a downside consideration, but the small seasonal sample does not support a separate adjustment."
      },
      {
        "kind": "math",
        "text": "Prior/update/interval: use a persistence prior shrunk equally toward the recent six-month level. Point = 0.5*60.114557 + 0.5*57.992099 = 59.053328%, rounded to 59.1%. Historical sample: 13 unrounded monthly shares, June 2025\u2013June 2026, giving 12 successive changes. Their mean is -1.062549 percentage points and their centered sum of squares is 412.612418; sigma = 6.124559 percentage points = sqrt(412.612418/11). Normal 80% baseline half-width = 1.28*sigma = 7.839435 points. August is two reporting months beyond June, so multiply by sqrt(2), giving 11.086636 points. This is 1.414 times the baseline. Momentum, one-off correction, and policy adjustments are zero. Bounds = 59.053328 +/- 11.086636 = 47.966692 to 70.139963%, rounded to 48.0\u201370.1%."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Upside risk: greater automatic matching or classification of renewals as ex parte could lift the successful-renewal share. Downside risk: more form-based renewals or continued ex parte undercounting could lower it. A substantial classification or cohort-composition shift could put the outcome outside the interval, above 70.1% or below 48.0%. A renewals-due denominator would also fall outside this interval because it defines a different statistic."
      },
